{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 923 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "f317ed41bea042e49c31ca09eeeffb9ff5b1b8b9530bbeb0716a314c890c5909" :edb/db-before-t 922 :edb/db-after-t 923 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534235 50 #inst "2026-10-11T18:03:58.980Z" 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186179740 1038 #edb/ref 17592186415312 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186179741 1038 #edb/ref 17592186415313 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186179741 1038 #edb/ref 17592186415315 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186179743 1038 #edb/ref 17592186415314 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186179865 1050 540.0 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186180022 1068 #edb/ref 17592186177801 13194139534235 17592186045417 false] [17592186180022 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415311 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186180022 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186180022 1071 "![](images/27/270e72ebedac3741e1b7086021b16dc0975ae9852d402673c8044a67f8f774fb.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and the vector field $F$, shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the **clockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $∮_{C}F \\cdot dr < 0$\n2. $∮_{C}F \\cdot dr > 0$\n3. $∮_{-C}F \\cdot dr > 0$" 13194139534235 17592186045417 false] [17592186180022 1071 "![](images/27/270e72ebedac3741e1b7086021b16dc0975ae9852d402673c8044a67f8f774fb.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the **clockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186180022 1074 "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves clockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](images/db/dbb6dbdfabccf7a94c67781210238c647e6f3a2e428cb79c4debdbff5e124720.png)\n\nSo, $Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$\n\n![](images/1c/1c5aa77b0a89e1fcb0782c9d969d3a81bbec47b004f07bd3a53ccd10e623ba6e.png)\n\nSo, $Γ={∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186415282 1080 "-25\\pi " 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186415282 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186415282 1083 #uuid "09f4c3d7-9a04-5668-b2e0-7bc01b46d0de" 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186415283 1080 "I and II only" 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186415283 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186415283 1083 #uuid "11d3f253-290b-54bb-babf-a6a6ff8978c0" 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186415284 1080 "II and III only" 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186415284 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186415284 1083 #uuid "152a2be2-a7fd-5859-a279-3e7945b3da34" 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186415285 1080 "-16\\pi " 13194139534235 17592186045417 true] [17592186415285 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534235 1759218